1
00:00:03,171 --> 00:00:07,694
Open Settings, Communication, Telephony, and choose the Soft Phone tab.

2
00:00:07,694 --> 00:00:11,982
Default telephony provider is the provider every call goes through.

3
00:00:11,982 --> 00:00:16,682
Allowed short codes lists the short numbers agents may dial, one per line,

4
00:00:16,682 --> 00:00:18,973
such as a carrier service number.

5
00:00:18,973 --> 00:00:24,671
Short numbers are refused unless they are listed, and emergency numbers can never be added.

6
00:00:25,174 --> 00:00:29,209
Enable the soft phone turns the phone on for authorized users.

7
00:00:29,209 --> 00:00:34,549
Show the soft phone on the admin dashboard puts the phone button on the admin pages.

8
00:00:34,549 --> 00:00:39,474
To show it on the front end, add the Soft Phone widget under Design, Widgets.

9
00:00:40,049 --> 00:00:44,569
Enable the diagnostics tab adds a Diagnostics tab to the phone.

10
00:00:44,569 --> 00:00:49,219
Recent calls to display sets how many calls the Recent tab lists.

11
00:00:49,733 --> 00:00:54,264
Default country is the country the phone's number box starts on, and it

12
00:00:54,264 --> 00:00:56,971
turns a national number into a full one.

13
00:00:56,971 --> 00:00:59,913
Accent color changes the color of the phone.

14
00:00:59,913 --> 00:01:02,913
Save, and the phone follows the new settings.

